      id: '17-faq',
      title: 'Frequently Asked Questions',
      titleTr: 'Sıkça Sorulan Sorular',
      content: `Q: What's the difference between Turning and Milling in this module?
A: Turning rotates the workpiece; Milling rotates the tool. This module analyzes operation type to select appropriate parameters.
Q: Does this module predict cutting parameters automatically?
A: No, it requires manual parameter input. The module then validates those parameters against machine and tool constraints.
Q: How do parameter relationships affect machining?
A: Speed, feed, and depth are interdependent. Changing one affects tool life, surface finish, and power requirements.
Q: Can I use this for drilling vs hole finishing?
A: Yes, select the operation type. Hole Finishing (honing, lapping) uses different parameter ranges and tools than Drilling.
Q: What happens if my parameters violate constraints?
A: The module shows which constraints are violated. Adjust parameters to stay within valid ranges for your machine and tool.
Q: What should I do after analysis?
A: Review results in the Surface Roughness and Tool Life modules. Then proceed to DFM for design compatibility check.`,
