      titleTr: 'Sıkça Sorulan Sorular',
      content: `Q: What inputs are required for cutting parameter calculation?
A: Material type, operation (turning/milling/drilling), tool type, and desired surface finish or tool life constraints.
Q: Can I fabricate cutting speed if my material isn't listed?
A: No. If material data is unavailable, don't estimate. Use reference materials with similar properties or contact engineering.
Q: How do machine limits affect parameter selection?
A: Machine limits (RPM, power, torque) constrain achievable speeds and feeds. The module checks your parameters against these limits.
Q: Why does the module show 'No valid parameters'?
A: This means your constraints are contradictory (e.g., very high speed + very low vibration). Relax one constraint or adjust inputs.
Q: Do tool geometry and coating affect cutting parameters?
A: Yes significantly. Geometry (rake, clearance) and coating (TiN, AlCrN) determine speed/feed ranges. Select matching tool before calculating.
Q: Should I validate these parameters before production?
A: Yes. Always test parameters on scrap material first. Use the Validation module to assess process robustness before production runs.`,
