    content: `Tool Life Model Assumptions:

Machine Assumptions:
• Machine spindle is in good condition (no runout/chatter)
• Machine is maintained to OEM specifications
• Machine is rigidly set up for this operation
• Spindle speed accuracy ±5% (typical)

Tool Assumptions:
• Tool is sharp (VB = 0 at start)
• Tool insert is correctly seated
• Tool holder has no wear or damage
• Tool geometry matches catalog specifications
• No tool breakage or fracture occurs

Coolant Assumptions:
• Coolant type is as specified (flooded, MQL, or dry)
• Coolant flow rate meets tool/operation requirements
• Coolant is cleaned/maintained (no swarf buildup)
• Coolant temperature is within operating range

Material Assumptions:
• Material composition is uniform (no hard spots)
• Material hardness matches input specification
• Material is delivered in standard condition
• No contaminant layers (rust, oxide scale) present

Operational Assumptions:
• Cutting parameters remain constant throughout operation
• Feed and speed are not manually adjusted
• No tool deflection or vibration occurs
• Operator does not interrupt cutting

Model Limitations:
• Taylor equation constants (C, n) are general references only
• No calibration for YOUR specific machine/tool combination
• Wear progression is assumed linear (not always true)
• Interrupted cuts, tool chatter, thermal growth not modeled
• This is conceptual model, not production prediction`,
