      title: 'Frequently Asked Questions',
      titleTr: 'Sıkça Sorulan Sorular',
      content: `Q: What are material libraries in MachiningPro?
A: Databases of material properties (hardness, strength, machinability) used to pre-populate parameters. Select material; module suggests speed/feed ranges.
Q: Can I add custom materials to the library?
A: Yes if your machine supports custom entries. Document hardness, tensile strength, machinability rating. Verify against test cuts before relying on estimates.
Q: What happens if material isn't in the library?
A: Use similar material as proxy (e.g., 316 stainless for unknown stainless). Verify with test cuts. Add to your custom library for future reference.
Q: How accurate are library suggestions?
A: Libraries provide starting points. Actual performance varies by machine condition, tool wear, setup. Always verify with test cuts before production runs.
Q: Can I share custom libraries across machines?
A: Yes, if your shop standardizes on tools and materials. Document parameters that work; build collective knowledge. Improves consistency across machines.
Q: How should I update libraries when I get new tools?
A: Run test cuts with new tool. Document speed, feed, tool life, finish. Update library entry for that tool/material combination. Accumulate your own data.`,
