      content: 'Related Modules and Sequential Context:\n\nTechnical Drawing Intelligence fits into this workflow sequence:\n\nUpstream Dependencies (Provide Input to This Module):\n→ Machines module: Equipment constraints and capabilities\n→ Materials module: Workpiece properties and compatibility\n→ Cutting Tools module: Tool geometry and selection criteria\n→ Cutting Parameters module: Speed and feed fundamentals\n\nThis Module:\n→ Technical Drawing Intelligence module: Explains mechanisms and relationships\n\nDownstream Applications (Use Output From This Module):\n→ Process Planning module: Sequence and resource scheduling\n→ DFM module: Design for manufacturability assessment\n→ Validation module: Testing and qualification procedures\n\nComplete Manufacturing Decision Workflow:\n1. Dashboard: Start workspace\n2. Machines: Understand equipment\n3. Materials: Understand workpiece properties\n4. Cutting Tools: Understand tool options\n5. Cutting Parameters: Understand parameter fundamentals\n6. Technical Drawing Intelligence: Understand technical drawing intelligence operation\n7. Process Planning: Plan manufacturing sequence\n8. DFM: Evaluate designability and manufacturability\n9. Technical Drawing Intelligence: Extract specifications\n10. Machine Capability: Assess machine qualification\n11. Validation: Run qualification testing\n12. Production deployment\n\nInformation Flow:\nMachine constraints → Parameter selection → Technical Drawing Intelligence analysis → Process planning → Validation testing\n\nDo NOT skip this sequence.\nDo NOT attempt production without completing all steps through Validation.\nEngineering judgment at each step is mandatory.',
